+## 3. Conflict reproduction (zero-credential, local)
+
+Divergence math on `origin/main` = f94c736:
+
+```
+branch tip   : 799a3a7  (bridge/bridge-20261028-js-dep-cve-gate)
+merge-base   : dc9e8b9  (= PR #1928 merge — the branch forked here)
+main ahead by: 1 commit (f94c736 = PR #1930 boundary sentinel)
+```
+
+`git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only origin/bridge/bridge-20261028-js-dep-cve-gate origin/main`:
+
+```
+5fa40331d174fa8744a27203cf1bb8e560970d2a
+scripts/ops/_INDEX.md
+
+Auto-merging scripts/ci/run_all_guards.py
+Auto-merging scripts/ops/_INDEX.md
+CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in scripts/ops/_INDEX.md
+```
+
+Per-side changes that collide:
+
+| Side | `scripts/ops/_INDEX.md` | New script it registered |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| main (f94c736, #1930) | 5 lines changed — added `boundary_contract_sentinel.py` entries, count 506→507 | `scripts/ci/boundary_contract_sentinel.py` |
+| PR #1932 (799a3a7) | 5 lines changed — added `js_dep_cve_guard.py` entries, count 506→507 | `scripts/ci/js_dep_cve_guard.py` |
+
+Both sides incremented the same counter line and inserted adjacent index rows, ending at the same total (507) with different content — a textbook generated-file content conflict. `scripts/ci/run_all_guards.py` is **not** conflicting: each side appended its own roster line, and git auto-merges them (verified below that both lines survive).
+
+## 4. Resolution path — proven locally on a throwaway merge
+
+Executed end-to-end on a scratch branch (since removed; commands are the record):
+
+1. `git checkout -b triage-test-merge origin/main && git merge origin/bridge/bridge-20261028-js-dep-cve-gate`
+   → `CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in scripts/ops/_INDEX.md` (only file, `UU`)
+2. `python3 scripts/ops/generate_script_index.py`
+   → `Wrote .../_INDEX.md — 508 scripts across 7 groups` (507 on main + the lane's `js_dep_cve_guard.py`), which resolves the conflict by regeneration — never hand-merge a `<!-- AUTO-GENERATED -->` file.
+3. Post-resolution invariants verified:
+   - `scripts/ci/run_all_guards.py` contains **both** roster wirings:
+     - L26 `["python", "scripts/ci/boundary_contract_sentinel.py", "--self-test"]` (from #1930)
+     - L30 `["python", "scripts/ci/js_dep_cve_guard.py", "--check"]` (from #1932)
+   - `scripts/ops/_INDEX.md` contains both new script entries (rg count = 2)
+4. Baseline sanity: regenerating the index on **pristine main** yields a timestamp-only diff (content byte-identical, `507 scripts (472 py · 30 sh · 5 js/mjs)` unchanged) — main's committed index is in sync, and the CI `--check` gate is timestamp-insensitive (otherwise every run would fail).
+
+**Lane-owner recipe (WO #1931 lane):**
+
+```
+git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main          # one conflict: scripts/ops/_INDEX.md
+python3 scripts/ops/generate_script_index.py        # regenerate — resolves the only conflict
+git add scripts/ops/_INDEX.md && git rebase --continue
+git push --force-with-lease                         # auto-lander then succeeds on next evaluation
+```
+
