+## 6. Auto-lander robustness observation (admin-gated, follow-up only)
+
+The landing job merges on green checks without consulting GitHub's mergeable state first. In a fleet where main moves multiple times per hour, the sequence *checks-pass → main-moves → merge-attempt → GraphQL conflict → exit 1 → federation dispatch → P2 mirror issue* will recur on every coincidence of landing timing. Two admin-side hardening options for `.github/` (protected path — not agent-actionable, recorded only):
+
+1. Pre-merge gate: query `mergeStateStatus` via GraphQL immediately before the squash-merge; proceed only on `CLEAN`, and on `CONFLICTING`/`DIRTY` exit 0 with a structured `lane-needs-rebase` annotation instead of an error page — the condition is routine churn, not an incident, and today it costs a red run + a P2 board item + a federation dispatch each time.
+2. Optionally pair with a bounded retry (one re-evaluation after a short backoff) for the case where the lane owner's rebase lands within the retry window.
+
+Neither option changes landing authority (constitutional gates only); both only change *how a known-unmergeable state is reported*. Deferred to the tower team.
